    "finishStory": {
      "markedParagraph": "After Joshua died, Israel repeatedly worshiped [idols] instead of the Lord. God allowed enemies to conquer Israel, and the people cried out for [help]. God sent the first [judge], a man named [Othniel]. He defeated their enemies, and the land enjoyed forty years of [peace]. After Othniel died, Israel again turned away, and evil King [Eglon] ruled over them. The Lord sent [Ehud], a left-handed rescuer who hid a [sword] on his right leg. Ehud defeated Eglon and [escaped] while the king's servants waited. Later, [Shamgar] rescued Israel by striking down 600 Philistines with an [oxgoad]. Through these rescues, God showed his [steadfast] love to his people.",
      "origin": "suggested",
      "teacherReviewRequired": true
    },
